  {
    "episode_id": 96850,
    "turn_file": "/shared/3/projects/podcasts/transcriptionQueue/turns/pol_appearance_episodes_interviews/9/6/96850.jsonl",
    "turn_idx": 2,
    "turn_text": "How do you ever want to welcome back to Moment of Truth, the podcast of American Moment. My name is Rob Sharma. I'm the president of American Moment, and this week it is just me in discussion with one of the most fantastic guests we've had on the show. Yet today we had on Senator Dr. Roger Marshall from the great state of Kansas, a long time coming interview, a real patriot who's distinguished himself in office over these last few years in particular. But before I get to that, Be sure as always to go to americanmoments.org. There you can find the 150 episode backlog of this podcast. You can find programs that we have upcoming. I think most relevant at this point is if you're coming to Washington DC this summer and want to be part of our lecture series AM Fridays where we'll have foundational public policy lectures on each of the important issues that matter on Capitol Hill every Friday, you can go to americanmoment.org slash AM Fridays and sign up for that if you're If you're a staffer and you want your interns to learn something useful and not just another seminar on free markets, then send them to that. And we also have the application open for our fall fellowship for American statecraft, first time ever that we've hosted that. I think applications close some time in May or June, so please make sure to apply for that soon. It's our first time doing a fall class. We want to be fantastic. This was the first year we did a spring class and they're wildly successful. I think half of them have already gotten their full-time jobs and we're still well over a month before the end of the program. So just really, really fantastic to be seeing our fellows constantly succeeding. You can also donate if you'd like to americanmoment.org slash donate. We always appreciate contributions that help keep the lights on around here and do more fantastic things. But today, my guest was Dr. Roger Marshall, who's a physician father, grandfather, and U.S. Senator for Kansas. He was a fifth generation farm kid growing up in Butler County. and he was the first in his family to attend college. He graduated from Butler County Community College, got a bachelor's degree from Kansas State, and a medical doctorate from the University of Kansas. He's just a brilliant, brilliant man. He practiced medicine for 25 years, served in the Army Reserves for seven years. delivered more than 5,000 babies, which turns out it's a really great way to be popular in politics. You know, Congressman Ron Paul also delivered like half of the babies in his congressional district. It's a great venue in politics. I think you get to know a lot of great families. And he's been incredibly involved with this church, many local businesses, and boards over the course of his life. And he decided to step into public service in 2015, ran for Congress, and then eventually for Senate, and has really distinguished himself, I think, over the last few years. One of the first topics we talk about in the show is talking about this new culture of real entrepreneurial activity that's come up in the United States Senate, where you have this cadre of a couple of members. You know, you think of JD Vance, Josh Hawley, Rand Paul, Mike Lee, Senator Marshall, Ted Cruz, Mike Braun, a couple others that are just putting lead on target every single day. Senator Ron Johnson, former guest on the show, and they seem to be having fun. They're aggressive. They've completely swept aside that old decrepit leadership structure. And I'm really excited to see what they do in the Senate. We talk about a lot of different topics on our show. Namely, what's super newsy this week is the incoming impeachment of Alejandro Mayorkas, what the strategy of conservatives in the Senate is going to be on that. We talk about Senator Marshall's bill on credit cards. He's got the bank spending, God knows how much money to try to say that he's some totalitarian communist for simply saying that the United States should not pay seven times the swipe fees that other countries do. We talk about Ukraine, we talk about his concerns about health. We get into some of the kind of dissident right health stuff, how he's thinking about health and nutrition, how he's not necessarily believing in us being a pill-popping culture that maybe people should focus on health and exercise above all. Just a really fantastic broad episode. I always like to say we really don't have a lot of politicians on this show because most politicians can't really stand up to an hour plus of scrutiny. But he really conducted himself fantastically. I feel like I could have talked with him for another hour or so. So we really hope you enjoy it. If you're a staffer and you believe your boss has what it takes to perform like Senator Marshall did, feel free to reach out. I promise you, the answer is not always going to be yes, but we're always happy to hear pitches for that. We'll go now to Senator Roger Marshall. Well, like I tell people very openly, we don't have a lot of elected officials on the show because very few of them can stand up to scrutiny at length, but you've really made a name for yourself doing some fantastic things in the Senate over the last few years. It's really been a joy to watch. I would love to just get a little bit of sense of where you're coming from. Tell us your story. Why did you first run for elected office? You have a pretty interesting background that I think our guests would like to hear.",
