  {
    "episode_id": 96850,
    "turn_file": "/shared/3/projects/podcasts/transcriptionQueue/turns/pol_appearance_episodes_interviews/9/6/96850.jsonl",
    "turn_idx": 11,
    "turn_text": "volunteer for any more boards and you need to stay home here a little bit more and help raise these children of yours. So at this point, we had two in college and actually want to finish college two in high school. And another year past, this is the year 2015, and we have our first grandchild. And that was the defining moment. We had one of those conversations like, you know, what's what's our legacy? What are we leaving for our grandchildren? And it was the worst economy in my professional lifetime. This is 2015 for a lot of reasons. And frankly, it was Barack Obama's policies that I think were driving the economy down. And There were so much regulations just exploding. The ACA, I had implemented the ACA. I had been in charge of overseeing our bank and the Dodd-Frank Act, Sony, with our economies horrible. And our grandson is born with $35,000 of debt. And she looks at me and says, this country's really broken. You like to fix things. It's now time for you to go. So we returned a couple phone calls of people that are recruited. And you know, those two phone calls turned into four, those turned into 16. And really God was blessing that. And I said, look, if we can raise $100,000 in the first month, then I think that we should keep going. And sure enough, we did and the rest is history. I was in the house for four years. And then our senior senator announces his retirement, Senator Pat Roberts, who'd been up here for 40 years, an incredible man. And we ran for that. And here we are, certainly feel like this is what God's plan is for our lives. When we went to rural America, we could have went anywhere in the country, but that was our mission field. We've done mission work all over the world, but we wanted to raise our kids in small town America, bring those things I talked about, the infertility. And now this is our mission. I think this is what God has called us to do. And my wife typically is the burning bush. She's the one that gets the messages from God that feel like this is our mission to try to leave this country better for the next generation.",
