  {
    "episode_id": 96850,
    "turn_file": "/shared/3/projects/podcasts/transcriptionQueue/turns/pol_appearance_episodes_interviews/9/6/96850.jsonl",
    "turn_idx": 16,
    "turn_text": "Absolutely. So, you know, the last few years in the Senate, I think that there's really been a second wind that a lot of the conservative senators have caught really coming into their own as a block. You know, I think I can think about five to 10 of you that that it seems like are always ganging up to do something cool or interesting to either gum up the works or get something good, good past or something bad killed. Tell me a little bit about just what that has been like. Is that an accurate assessment? Do you feel like you guys are working together better than you have before? What's that been like to be part of the generational changing of the guard in the Senate?",
