  {
    "episode_id": 96850,
    "turn_file": "/shared/3/projects/podcasts/transcriptionQueue/turns/pol_appearance_episodes_interviews/9/6/96850.jsonl",
    "turn_idx": 18,
    "turn_text": "I certainly hope so, and I want to talk more about what you're hoping to see in terms of the leadership of the Senate a little bit later, but I think it's important to frame it in the context of some of these big failures that have happened over these last few years, namely the border deal being I think the biggest manifestation of this old way of doing things in Washington. Luckily, it seems to have fallen apart, but just give us your narrative on what it was like to be a senator that wasn't brought into that insider process and what it was like to team up with the other conservative senators to say, no, this is not enough.",
