    "turn_idx": 21,
    "turn_text": "and but drive in their own political agenda. And our leadership was in bed with that. I don't we could talk about that more, but but specifically that was their lever. And there's a group of us that would say, look, I really stand beside Israel. It's real important to me spiritually, personally, and politically to support Israel. At this point in time, you know, a friend in need is a friend indeed. And they're in need right now. So let's support Israel, let's not abandon them in their moment of need. And by the way, they're on the right side of this. And Amos is on the wrong side. They're still chanting death to America. But you're right. They, they, what they brought forth to us, for the border deal, what made it worse? I was hopeful. I tried to remain supportive, though they weren't going to tell us anything was totally done in the dark. And, and I think we could have, we had one person negotiating for us. And this is a complex topic. I've done several business deals. I would never go into a business deal with the secretary of DHS who's doing a horrible job. So he's in there making the deal along with 15 of Biden's people and three or four Democrats. And we have one Republican at the table. You know, I want to go in there with my guns loaded. I want Ted Cruz just to beat the hell out of them. Every time they say something stupid. I want Mike Lee beside me, you know, working on the technical legal part of this saying, wait a second. That's not what this deal is showing here and bring all those minds together. So we wasted these incredible minds that we have. We've got the best legal experience up here. I don't know, a handful of them have clerked at the Supreme Court, all great lawyers in there. I'm a doctor, I'm gonna get the consultation. So we didn't put our best foot forward. It was set up for failure to begin with. And I blame that on our leadership.",
