    "turn_idx": 67,
    "turn_text": "It's a smart point and it's one that we're not really set up to respond to. We have a highly developed military, very technologically advanced, but you compare our cyber capabilities to any of these other countries. It's a night and day difference. Their most talented coders and hackers end up working for their state cyber commands, whereas in our country, they go work in the private sector, which is great, but it means that we're highly, highly vulnerable. It's interesting, it feels like healthcare policy is the thing that no one in Washington wants to talk about, because it seems like every time anyone tries to do anything, it blows up in their face. But there's a chance that we might have unified Republican control of Congress in the White House in the coming years. And I'm sure people are gonna start hitting you up and",
