    "turn_idx": 80,
    "turn_text": "But just giving up things like that would lose 10% of their body weight. And especially if you throw that along with just walking for 20 minutes. So I think it's going to be executing a simple plan well. This is not rocket science. So how do we execute this plan? I've tried to get the Surgeon General to be more active. What type of warning would we put on a 32 ounce soda? is that good, you know, this is dangerous to, I don't know. So I'm looking for solutions. I do think that this younger generation though is much more attuned to this. And they're hearing it. So we need to be preaching that message up here too, that you don't need a, I sort of 20 years ago, I said all of a sudden people want fast food medicine. Really? All of a sudden, I get to see this shift in people saying they just want to call me and get a prescription to fix whatever their problem was. I feel depressed today. Can you just call me in an antidepressant for a couple of weeks? Oh, I'm having problems studying in college right now. Can you get me one of those drugs that help you",
