    "turn_idx": 108,
    "turn_text": "As a final question, Senator, in all the topics we've discussed, whether it's Ukraine, immigration, the fentanyl, health, you've exhibited, I think, real interesting heterodoxy vis-a-vis what might be the mainstream big business corporate Republican position. But there's one piece of legislation in particular that I think really demonstrates that, and that's what you've been doing on the credit cards. What's the problem with the credit cards? I feel like I read in some libertarian rags somewhere that you're trying to take away my points. Why are you trying to take away my points? What's going on here and why have you made DC so angry?",
