    "turn_idx": 120,
    "turn_text": "Well, and it's only going to get worse, right? Because the big trend I see with people my age and younger, they don't carry cash. So like I remember growing up, you know, there'd be, you'd go to a gas station and it'd say, you know, any order under any purchase under $5. It's cash only or something like that or an additional fee. As that becomes less and less tenable because Gen Z isn't carrying cash. It's going to squeeze these small shops even more. And then the only thing that can survive is the big uh, uh, uh, uh, chains, you know, Walmart and Target, et cetera, which is not, I want to, I would love to live in a world where you only walk down a downtown and, you know, mid-sized American city that you actually see local places and it's not the same 20 brands on every single street. Um, so I, I appreciate you for thinking in a more creative way about this. Um, you know, Senator, we always like to ask our guests to finish out what, um, what's the thing they're paying attention to that no one else is right now. Um, a lot of the, leaders in this populist movement. They tend to be Cassandra's for something that everyone will be talking about three years later. What's that issue for you, something that you believe that no one else does, and how can people follow all of what you're thinking and working on?",
